// The interesting case: an element-wise op feeding three aggregations. Right now
// abs runs over the matrix once, then min, max and mean each scan the result
// again -- four passes in total. The fusion work computes all three stats while
// abs is already touching every element, so it becomes one pass instead of four.
//
//   daphne --explain property_inference --explain kernels 03_fusion_target.daph

X = fill(-5.0, 8, 8);
Y = abs(X);
print(aggMin(Y));
print(aggMax(Y));
print(mean(Y));
